{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Particle Emitter Birth and Limit.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Particle Emitter Birth and Limit.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"particle emitter birth and limit particle emitter birth and limit","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Particle Emitter Birth and Limit.md","fileName":"Particle Emitter Birth and Limit.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Particle Emitter Birth and Limit","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Particle and Destruction VFX]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Particle and Destruction VFX","Particle Motion Forces and Lifetime","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Particle Emitter Birth and Limit.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Particle Emitter Birth and Limit.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"particle emitter birth and limit particle emitter birth and limit","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Particle Emitter Birth and Limit.md","fileName":"Particle Emitter Birth and Limit.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Particle Emitter Birth and Limit","heading":"Particle Emitter Birth and Limit","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An emitter defines where particles begin, how quickly they are born, and the total number that may exist. A birth rate of one per frame spreads a fixed limit across time; a birth rate equal to the limit releases the whole burst on one frame. That difference helps distinguish a continuous fountain from an explosion. A nozzle determines the initial arrangement, while generation can be triggered by time, keyframe, or an event such as a collision. Later appearance depends on [[Particle Motion Forces and Lifetime]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Particle and Destruction VFX","Particle Motion Forces and Lifeti